# rfc-001-authentication.mdc

## Title
RFC 001 – Authentication & Role Assignment

## Summary
This RFC outlines the implementation details for the authentication system of the educational video platform, including user registration, login, JWT session handling, and post-registration role assignment.

---

## Goals
- Secure user authentication
- Support both email/password and magic link login
- Basic role assignment after signup (default: `User`)
- Role elevation (to `Team Lead` or `Admin`) managed by Admin

## Supabase Auth Setup
- **Auth Provider**: Supabase built-in auth
- **Login Methods**:
  - Email + Password (primary)
  - Magic Link (optional/phase 2)
- **Session**: JWT-based (stored in localStorage/cookies via Supabase client SDK)

## Tables
### `profiles`
Custom user data is stored here (linked to Supabase `auth.users`)
| Field         | Type      | Description                     |
|---------------|-----------|---------------------------------|
| id            | uuid      | PK (matches auth.users.id)      |
| email         | text      | Redundant for easy access       |
| role          | text      | ENUM: 'admin', 'team-lead', 'user', 'guest' |
| created_at    | timestamp |                                |

### `roles`
Static lookup table (optional)
| Role        |
|-------------|
| admin       |
| team-lead   |
| user        |
| guest       |

## Role Logic
- On registration, all users are inserted into `profiles` with role = `user`
- Admin can elevate a user's role via Admin Panel
- Guest access is handled via public routes (not logged in)
- Supabase Row-Level Security (RLS) policies control access to data based on role

## Frontend Integration
- Use Supabase client SDK for auth methods
- On successful login/register:
  - Fetch profile via RPC or `select * from profiles where id = user.id`
  - Store session in localStorage using Supabase methods
- Provide client-side context for role and session state

## API Endpoints (if needed)
- `/api/auth/profile` → Returns full user profile from Supabase
- `/api/auth/role/update` → (Admin only) Update role of a user

## UI Elements
- Login/Register Page
- Role-based route guards (Admin Panel, Course Builder, etc.)
- Toast notifications on login/register failure

## Security
- Enforce HTTPS
- Supabase RLS on all sensitive tables
- Passwords handled by Supabase (not stored locally)

## Timeline
**Sprint 1**
- Setup Supabase project and connect to frontend
- Create `profiles` table and seed roles
- Implement login/register forms
- Implement role-based frontend layout loading

